# A THIRD KNOWN-STOP, and a THIRD project, for the reason the first two already established: a
# build stops at the FIRST error, so two known-stops sharing a project means the second one's
# message is never reached — it would assert nothing while looking like it asserts something.
#
# IT USED TO PIN A DIFFERENT STOP, and that history is why this file was renamed rather than
# rewritten. It was `native_match_fat_known_stop`, pinning
# *"fat-pointer receiver `match-expression` not yet lowered"*: `lower_fat_expr` accepted a CLOSED
# set of fat-pointer (ptr+len) producers — string literal, array literal, bound local, struct
# field, `if`-expression (degrau 5), direct call (degrau call-gordo) — and a `match`-VALUE was not
# one of them, so every `str`-returning function whose body is a match stopped. 0.3.1.0 DEGRAU 5
# CLOSED THAT (`lower_match_fat`), and this fixture did exactly what its own note asked of it: it
# went red the day the gap closed.
#
# THE PROMOTION WENT TO THE CORPUS, NOT INTO THIS FILE. The positive claim now lives in
# `own_native.tkr` as `fat_match_value`, which asserts the `str` shape, the `[]T` shape (whose
# length differs per arm) and an arm that re-assigns an enclosing scalar — off a build that already
# exists. This project cannot make that claim itself, because ONE STOP DEEPER its `speak_or` hits
# another:
#
#   `native backend N1: fat-pointer interface-dispatch result not yet lowered (N2)`
#
# The arm calls `v.speak()` — a VIRTUAL dispatch whose result is `str` — and `lower_call_fat`'s own
# narrower named stop refuses a fat result arriving through a vtable. A different family (the call
# ABI, not the producer set), which is why the project was RENAMED instead of retired: it still
# pins a real, reachable, first-in-the-build stop, and the name now says which one.
#
# NOT a bad fixture, by the owner's own test: nothing declares a loose `null`; both bindings are
# annotated `Animal_sbmd | null` and receive what that type accepts. The stop is the backend's.
#
# PROMOTE the day the fat interface-dispatch result lands: back to `When built and run` /
# `Then exit = 42`, source back into `bulk`.
Feature: native backend — a fat (`str`) result through INTERFACE DISPATCH (KNOWN-STOP, .32)

  Scenario: a `str`-returning virtual method called through its base stops honestly
    When compilation fails
    Then diagnostic = "fat-pointer interface-dispatch result not yet lowered"
